{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Simulations","title":"Simulations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration"]},{"anchor":"Time","title":"Time","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"]},{"anchor":"States","title":"States","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" owns a world and a set of schedules, each named by a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". You add","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems to the schedules by label, then call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" once a frame with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time that passed. The simulation decides which schedules run:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup"},{"text":" runs once, before the first frame.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate"},{"type":"text","text":" runs once for every fixed timestep of time that has passed, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics and other rate-sensitive rules advance by the same amount each run, however uneven the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frames are."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update"},{"type":"text","text":" runs once a frame."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and systems:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double }","struct FixedSteps: Resource { var count = 0 }","enum GameState: States { case menu, playing, paused }","","\/\/\/ Moves each entity by its velocity over one fixed timestep.","@System","struct Physics {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>, _ fixedTime: ResourceReader<FixedTime>) {","        let seconds = fixedTime.value.timestep \/ .seconds(1)","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx * seconds","        }","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Counts the runs of the schedule it is in.","@System","struct CountSteps {","    func run(_ steps: ResourceWriter<FixedSteps>) {","        steps.value.count += 1","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Spawns a ball at the origin.","@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(commands: inout Commands) {","        commands.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example runs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Physics"},{"text":" on a fixed timestep of 1\/64 second, the default. A frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of 50 milliseconds covers three whole timesteps, so the ball moves three times:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","","var simulation = Simulation(world)","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics() }","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"States","text":"States","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A state type is a type, usually an enumeration, that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the screens of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game, or the phases of a simulation. Add one to a simulation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The simulation keeps the current state in the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource; to change it, a system sets "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and the change applies at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next frame. Entering, leaving and moving between states run schedules of their own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes a run condition that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in one state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example spawns a ball on entering the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"playing"},{"type":"text","text":" state and moves it only while the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game is in that state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var simulation = Simulation()","simulation.add(state: GameState.menu)","simulation.add(to: .onEnter(GameState.playing)) { SpawnBall() }","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics().runIf(inState(GameState.playing)) }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","simulation.world.resources[NextState<GameState>.self].set(.playing)","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.resources[CurrentState<GameState>.self].state)","\/\/ Prints \"playing\"","for (_, position) in simulation.world.query(Position.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SimulationModule","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SimulationModule"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"SimulationModule"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/simulationmodule"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with states that switch systems on and off.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","role":"collection","title":"SimulationModule","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/add(state:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"add","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"state","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Adds a state type to the simulation, starting in the given state.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"add(state:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/add(state:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/fixedUpdate":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once for each fixed timestep of elapsed time."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"fixedUpdate","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/fixedupdate","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fixedUpdate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/inState(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a run condition that holds when a world’s current state is the given state."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"inState(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/instate(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inState","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> (","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/update(elapsed:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Advances the simulation by one frame."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"update(elapsed:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/update(elapsed:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"update"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"elapsed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/CurrentState":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the state a simulation is in.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/currentstate","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"CurrentState"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onTransition(from:to:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"onTransition"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation changes from one given state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to another.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"onTransition(from:to:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/ontransition(from:to:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/startup":{"abstract":[{"text":"The label of the schedule that runs once, before the first frame.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/startup","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"startup","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"startup"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/NextState":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NextState","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the state a simulation enters at the start of its next frame."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NextState","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/nextstate","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NextState","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel":{"title":"ScheduleLabel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleLabel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel","abstract":[{"text":"The name of a schedule in a simulation.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/update":{"title":"update","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"update"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","precise